{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1311358-v20-house-gwydion-boon","id":1311358,"title":"v20 House Gwydion Boon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-11T00:29:45-07:00","id":1311358,"title":"v20 House Gwydion Boon","content":"Hello ! I'm currently playing a game of Changeling the dreaming v20, we're enjoying ourselves but the topic of Houses boon came and...well House Gwydion boon seems a bit, let's say... meh-ish, having the opportunity to roll to see if someone is lying to you ? Well anyone can do that right ? Am i missing something ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T03:14:42-07:00","id":1311371,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it is a bit problematic depending on how you handle mundane lying and noticing if someone is lying. And how you interpret the actual Boon. <br /> For background information in 2nd edition it was per+ken roll with a difficulty of the liar\u2019s WP and in 2nd ed WP cost 2 freebies per dot, meaning that willpower scores tended to be on the low side and you needed only one success on your Boon roll to sense a lie.<br /> <br /> Now if you interpret the C20 Boon with all that in mind you could say it means you roll your Per+Ken Vs a difficulty of liar\u2019s Man+Sub with you needing a single success to sense the lie, then the Boon becomes useful as it tends to be easier to see through good liar\u2019s with it than your basic Per+Emp Vs Man+Sub resisted rolls. Because with the Boon in this interpretation it doesn\u2019t matter how well the liar rolls.<br /> <br /> If it still feel\u2019s too meh-ish even with that just let Gwydion automatically sense lies, it should make them even more infuriating to work with, and make Eiluned even more infuriating for Gwydion to have around. But his latter option puts you firmly on House Rule country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T18:44:30-07:00","id":1311472,"title":"","content":"Yeah I totally misread it as Gwydion auto succeed vs Mundane lies and only have to roll if its vs some sort of magical lie power, which I will probably stick with for house rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}